        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "topological-mass-transient-localisation-proof.md:28-44 — the proof's key equation ‖∏_i MI∫_{D_i}‖ = Σ_i ‖MI∫_{E_i}‖ asserts that the norm of a *product* of group-valued multiplicative integrals equals the *sum* of the per-factor norms. For a general (non-abelian) group-valued MI this is false; norm-of-product = sum-of-norms holds only after an abelian log/character map, which the proof gestures at ('commute up to the central band') but does not establish.",
        "notes": "The lemma being proved (topological-mass-transient-localisation.md:7-18) is exactly this additivity. The corresponding Lean (QOU/LiftingDescent/tm_transient_localisation.lean:50-52) states it as MItotal = Σ MIdiv i with NO hypotheses — which is literally false (N=0, MItotal=1 ⇒ 1=0) and only 'provable' via sorry. The narrative proof's product→sum step is the load-bearing claim and is not justified for non-abelian MI."
